      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While specific clothing or accessories are never definitive evidence of criminal intent, certain visual indicators can warrant closer observation. Particular styles of heavily layered, bulky, or obscuring clothing, such as large hoods or extreme baggy silhouettes, can be used to hide items or intent. Be alert to noticeable, repeated displays of symbols, colors, or wearing specific branded accessories known to be associated with local affiliations. Ultimately, these visual cues should be used as triggers to increase observation, not as immediate cause for action.",
